    <GaugingStation location="Dalry" name="Garnock" number="83002">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">A velocity-area station downstream of the Muirhead and Camphill Reservoirs.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">After a long period of closure, the station was reopened on 21/11/2014 to inform flood management. The new station infrastructure is situated on top of the original station plinth. The station is gauged up to 2.657m, with a measured flow of 57.7 cumecs. The rating has been extended by flow modelling to increase the confidence of flood estimation. The new station has a different datum from the original site.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">River section 0.8km d/s of Dalry. Station added to peak flows dataset in September 2023 (WINFAP Files v12).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Runoff substantially reduced by PWS exports from u/s reservoirs.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff"/>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Gaugings up to 2.657m and flow modelling provide some confidence in the flood estimations." suitable="Yes" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
